  "human_summary": "Formalized: the named PG23 theorem surface is proved for the pinned arXiv source. The appendix support observations prove support-interior CDF strictness, positive powered-CDF range, and positive open-interval mass. The concrete continuum type laws directly produce stable/clearing cutoff characterizations and unique shared cutoffs. From literal choice and clearing identities, Lean proves the probability formula proposition, the lower monoculture cutoff, polyculture's limiting sorting and welfare, monoculture's invariant and strictly suboptimal welfare, all three matching-comparison clauses, the shared-cutoff and scalar-bridge differential-access probability formulas, mono/poly differential-access Equal Cutoffs, and the finite Nash no-deviation row for expected favorite-success payoff. The experimental section and conclusion are empirical/narrative rather than theorem targets. No theorem-facing record packages any of these conclusions.",
